  ('ECO 201', 'Microeconomic Theory I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('MTH 211', 'Set, Logic and Algebra', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'Elective. Introduction to the language and concepts of modern mathematics; topics include: Basic set theory, mappings, relations, equivalence and other relations, Cartesian product. Binary logic, methods of proof. Binary operations, algebraic structures, semi-groups, rings, integral domains, fields, Homomorphism. Number systems; properties of integers, rationals, real and complex numbers.', '["Introduction to the language and concepts of modern mathematics", "Topics include: Basic set theory, mappings, relations, equivalence and other relations, Cartesian product", "Binary logic, methods of proof", "Binary operations, algebraic structures, semi-groups, rings, integral domains, fields, Homomorphism", "Number systems", "Properties of integers, rationals, real and complex numbers"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('MTH 221', 'Real Analysis', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'Elective. Bounds of real numbers, convergence of sequences of numbers. Monotone convergence of series. Absolute and conditional convergence of series, and rearrangements. Completeness of reals and incompleteness of rationals. Continuity and differentiability of functions. Rolle''s and mean-value theorems for differentiable functions. Taylor series.', '["Bounds of real numbers, convergence of sequences of numbers", "Monotone convergence of series", "Absolute and conditional convergence of series, and rearrangements", "Completeness of reals and incompleteness of rationals", "Continuity and differentiability of functions", "Rolle''s and mean-value theorems for differentiable functions", "Taylor series"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('ECO 281', 'Structure of Nigerian Economy I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('PHY 251', 'Electromagnetism I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective. Electrostatics. Gauss'' Law. Fields of charge distribution, methods of images. Dielectrics, Polarization. Electric current, current density. D.C. network theory. Ampere''s Law, magnetic fields of simple circuits. Faraday''s law of induction, self and mutual inductances, inductively coupled circuits. Transients in capacitive and inductive circuits. A.C. circuit analysis. Magnetization and hysteresis. Permanent magnetism - Diamagnetism, Paramagnetism and ferromagnetism. Lorentz force. Hall Effect. Maxwell''s equation - electromagnetic waves.

Prerequisite: PHY 118 or PHY 124', '["Electrostatics", "Gauss'' Law", "Fields of charge distribution, methods of images", "Dielectrics, Polarization", "Electric current, current density", "D.C", "Network theory", "Ampere''s Law, magnetic fields of simple circuits", "Faraday''s law of induction, self and mutual inductances, inductively coupled circuits", "Transients in capacitive and inductive circuits", "A.C", "Circuit analysis", "Magnetization and hysteresis", "Permanent magnetism - Diamagnetism, Paramagnetism and ferromagnetism", "Lorentz force", "Hall Effect", "Maxwell''s equation - electromagnetic waves"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('MTH 216', 'Elementary Differential Equation I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Statistics', '200 Level', 'second', 3, 'The Statistics course module prints this title against MTH 216; the Mathematics department lists MTH 216 as Linear Algebra II. Quoted as printed. Representations of linear transformations by matrices, change of bases, equivalence and similarity. Determinants. Eigenvalues and eigenvectors. Minimum and characteristic polynomials of a linear transformation. Cayley-Hamilton theorem, bilinear and quadratic forms, orthogonal diagonalization. Canonical forms.', '["Representations of linear transformations by matrices, change of bases, equivalence and similarity", "Determinants", "Eigenvalues and eigenvectors", "Minimum and characteristic polynomials of a linear transformation", "Cayley-Hamilton theorem, bilinear and quadratic forms, orthogonal diagonalization", "Canonical forms"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
